From 694fe56d5d3d0a0f951664c8eb8f26403eb71a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?= <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:25:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] wayland: Advertise the GPU render node when the KMS
 device has none

On many ARM SoCs the display controller muffin drives (sun4i-drm, rockchip,
meson...) and the GPU (panfrost, lima, etnaviv...) are separate DRM devices.
The KMS device has no render node and rendering goes through Mesa's
kmsro/renderonly layer, so drmGetRenderDeviceNameFromFd() returns NULL:
wl_drm is then not advertised at all and dma-buf v4 advertises the card
node as main device. Mesa clients can't find a GPU ("failed to get driver
name for fd -1") and silently fall back to llvmpipe.

Fall back to the lowest-numbered render node in that case, which is the
GPU the kernel registered first, and use it for both wl_drm and the
dma-buf v4 main device.

Also, for the backport onto 6.4.x: add meta_renderer_native_get_primary_gpu()
(as in mutter) and a should_send_modifiers() that keeps 6.4.x behaviour of
always advertising the real importable modifiers.

Tested on an Orange Pi 4A (Allwinner T527: sun4i-drm + panfrost).

Co-authored-by: AI Agent
